AUDIO: 'let\'s say, the K sampler, for example. We can see obviously that if we just hover over this specific node that our inputs are coming from anything everywhere. All right, number six on our list today is the CR prompt list node and this is one of my personal favorites'

[04:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'of all time. So, this one is not flashy at all, and that\'s exactly why it\'s on the list. This is one of those nodes that quietly ends up in every single workflow I build because it solves a problem every one of you has hit before.'

[05:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'You\'ve got a prompt and you want to run variations of it. Maybe you want to test five different outfits, 10 different locations, 20 different camera angles, whatever it might be. And what do most people do? They cue a generation, wait'

[05:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'for it to finish, click into the prompt box, edit the text, cue the generation again, wait again, edit it again. And in my opinion, that\'s just an absolutely miserable way to work. So with CR prompt'

[05:26] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: ComfyUI interface displaying the "CR Prompt List" node with multi-line text input.
AUDIO: 'list, you get as many multi-line text fields as you want, and every line you type is its own separate prompt. So instead of one prompt, this node is holding an entire list of prompts. So, when you fill out this multi-line text'

[05:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'field here, you can fill it with as many prompts as you\'d like, separated by just pressing enter on your keyboard or a line break. You hit run and you walk away, and it just chews through your entire list of prompts one by one without you touching anything. And'

[05:52] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'there\'s a couple things that you can do with this node to get different results. You\'ll see here that there\'s a prepen text and an apen text option, which means that anything that I type in this prepen text box here will be added to the body of prompts that I select here.'

[06:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'So, I\'m going to fill this out and show you exactly how it formats and outputs these prompts with prepend added to it and apen added to it. And we will see our result right here in this previous'

[06:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'text box. So, as you can see, I\'ve added five very basic prompts into the multi-line body text here. And I\'ve added a prepen text, a woman, and an apen text wearing a sundress. Now, you'

[06:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'can see here that I have forgot to put a space after a woman and a space before wearing a sundress. And I did this on purpose to showcase that you need to be very specific with your prompting,'

[06:43] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: ComfyUI showing the "CR Prompt List" node with prepend and append text applied to prompts.
AUDIO: 'obviously, because it\'s not going to add spaces for you if you forget to put them there. So, I\'m going to add a space to the end of a woman and a space before wearing a sundress and then recatinate these strings here. And you can see that'

[06:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'they properly are formatted now without any grammatical errors. This prepend and a text is especially useful if you have a character or Laura that you attach to a workflow. For example, let\'s just say'

[07:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that you have a trigger word for your Laura, your Laura, a woman. Now I can attach the Laura trigger word to every single one of these prompts that I pass'

[07:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'through my workflow. And I\'ll just regenerate these. And you can see that now our trigger word for our character Laura is attached to each one of these prompts. So now if you want to implement these prompts that you\'ve just created with your CR prompt list into your workflow, all you need to do is take the'

[07:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'prompt output and wire it right into the text input box in your positive prompt section of your workflow. And then you can just run your workflow and it\'ll iterate through all of these and create a generation for each one of these'

[07:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'prompts that you have. And the only thing that separates these prompts is pressing enter on the keyboard. So I can add as much as I want to this prompt. But until I press enter, it\'s not going to create another generation. So now'

[07:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that I press enter, that will be a sixth generation if I wanted to do that. But I\'m not going to do that. I\'m just going to run this workflow with these five to demonstrate that it iterates through all five in one run. And just like that, all five of them have ran in a single batch.'

