[21:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the eye looks just not right. Right. So, that leads us to our final set of nodes. Here we have face detailer, which is from the Comfy Impact Pack. So, if'

[22:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you\'ve been doing AI image generation for any amount of time, you have seen busted faces, melted features, misaligned eyes, weird mouths, just AI hallucinations and artifacting that is pretty common with AI image generation.'

[22:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'And for a long time, the answer was to just regenerate and hope for better. But, Face Detailer is the answer to that problem. And you get more value out of every every generation because while something from your original generation, for example, this blinking eye here may'

[22:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'be messed up, passing it through these detailer nodes can fix that. So here\'s exactly what it does. It automatically detects every face in your image, crops in on it, runs a separate focus sampling'

[22:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'pass at a higher resolution just on the face, and then blends the result back into the original image. So, your sampler never saw the face clearly the first time maybe, but that\'s because it was probably working on the whole image at once, and the face was just a few'

[23:03] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: ComfyUI showing the "FaceDetailer" node's parameters.
AUDIO: 'pixels in a larger scheme of pixels, which is your entire image or person or scenario setting, whatever it may be. So, the face detailer gives it a second shot with full attention just on the face, really focusing in on those'

[23:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'pixels. And you can detail more than just faces. There are models, very small models called ultralytics detectors, BBOX detectors, segment detectors. But for example purposes, I am using the'

[23:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'BBOX face detector by Yolo V and the BBOX eye detector. It\'s called Eiffel V2. I am not sure who made it. My apologies on that. What this does is even though these are both technically'

[23:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'called face detailer nodes, if we attach these detectors individually to their own face detailer nodes, it will segment just the eyes or just the face or whatever else you may want to detect.'

[23:56] [scene:talk]
